  "body": "The Wire Contour operation accepts a 3 degree taper. Setting the same parameter to zero returns an unknown field error.\n\nWith a mounted Wire EDM machine, use add_operation with a Wire Contour and a valid wire condition. Set params.taper_deg to 0. The command refuses the field. Omitting it creates the vertical operation. Create a 3 degree taper and use edit_operation with params.taper_deg set to 0. That command also refuses the field.\n\nThe error starts with: bad params patch: unknown field taper_deg. The wire operation data omits the default zero on save. The patch validator reads that omission as a dropped field.\n\nDone means: The add and edit commands accept a zero taper for Wire Contour. A test clears an existing taper to zero and checks that genuinely unknown fields still fail.\n",
